\item{\code{"mean"}}{Takes every bar. \code{"se"} and \code{"sd"} are one standard error
and one standard deviation either side, and \code{"ci"} is Student's interval
at \code{conf_level}: \code{\link[stats:qt]{stats::qt()}} on \code{n - 1} degrees of freedom times the
standard error.}
\item{\code{"median"}}{Takes \code{"ci"} only, the notch interval
\verb{median +/- 1.58 * IQR / sqrt(n)}. That is the same interval
\code{\link[=draw_grouped_boxplot]{draw_grouped_boxplot()}} returns as \code{median_confidence_stats}, so a bar
and the notch of the box beside it are the same width on the same data.
\code{"se"} and \code{"sd"} describe the observations' spread about their mean and
are refused here rather than drawn around a median they are not about.}
\item{Everything else}{Takes \code{"none"}. A height that is itself a spread, a
count or a shape has no second quantity for an interval to be about.}
